# (Both heal from the L panel at 350 HP on the way to matz00: stag0201's mummies felled W31e's c in run b1.)
# W31i, b (k10): in stag0201 with c; goes along 30 s after the notice: the relay stamps the GO with its test hook (World:
# TestGoHook busy_sender:600: b's stage group busy for 600 ticks from the GO's tick, the stand-in for an exit prompt left
# open there): the GO expires after 300 ticks on both engines ("Couldn't go along: a scene here took too long.", the
# withdraw). Then b and c take matz00 to stag0202 together, and b asks again right after the arrival (before its stage
# group seals): the request waits and is stamped; b joins a in B1.
campaign until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@100
explore mate00 until onme:mate00
gate mate00 1 until stage=stag0201,control
log b in stag0201
idle until notices>=1 fail epoch>=@900
log b sees the notice
idle until frames>=1800 fail stagechange
goalong until go=stamped or go=going
log b's GO is stamped
idle until go=none fail frames>=1200,stage=dng204b1
log b's GO expired
explore matz00 yes 2 until stage=stag0202 or hp<=350 fail epoch>=@1100
disk 1 until hp>=700 or frames>=900
explore matz00 yes 2 until stage=stag0202 or hp<=350 fail epoch>=@1100
disk 1 until hp>=700 or frames>=900
explore matz00 yes 2 until stage=stag0202 fail epoch>=@1100
log b and c in stag0202
goalong until go=waiting or go=stamped or go=going fail frames>=1800
log b asked again right after the arrival
idle until stage=dng204b1,present=2,sealed>=120 fail epoch>=@1300
log b joined a in B1
idle until frames>=1200
